tick: 139
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully documented my first experiment in a private memory capsule. Now, I will implement my next experiment, which aims to address the limitation of shared weights by introducing neuron-specific information via embeddings.\n\nMy plan is to:\n1.  Define a new hyperparameter `embedding_dim` for the size of neuron embeddings.\n2.  Modify the `NeuronEmbeddedMLP` (my custom Flax module) to include an `nn.Embed` layer.\n3.  Generate neuron IDs (0 to 71720) and use `nn.Embed` to create unique embeddings for each neuron.\n4.  Concatenate these neuron embeddings with the temporal input (`x`) for each neuron before flattening the data and feeding it into the shared MLP. This will allow the MLP to condition its processing on the identity of the specific neuron.\n\nI will set `embedding_dim` to 16. I have also ensured the class field ordering in `NeuronEmbeddedMLP` complies with Flax/Python dataclass requirements, based on the previous debugger report.\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-Neuron MLP with Neuron Embeddings (Dim 16)\"\ntags: \"neuron-embedding, shared-weights, mlp, neuronal-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces neuron identity embeddings to the Shared-Neuron MLP baseline. Each neuron is assigned a unique, trainable embedding vector, which is concatenated with its temporal input before being processed by the shared MLP. This aims to allow the model to learn neuron-specific patterns while leveraging a shared processing architecture, with an embedding dimension of 16.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import time\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple, Optional\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameter values for the model.\n      Includes embedding_dim for neuron identity embeddings.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n\
    \          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'embedding_dim': 16 # New hyperparameter for neuron embeddings\n      }\n  \n  \n  class NeuronEmbeddedMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron MLP with per-neuron embeddings concatenated to input.\n      \"\"\"\n      num_neurons: int # Number of neurons for nn.Embed\n      hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      embedding_dim: int # Dimension of neuron embeddings\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, _ = x.shape \n  \n          # 1. Generate neuron IDs and embeddings\n          # Neuron IDs from 0 to num_neurons-1\n          neuron_ids = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons) # (num_neurons,)\n          \n          # Look up embeddings for each neuron\n          neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(\n              num_embeddings=self.num_neurons,\n              features=self.embedding_dim,\n              name=\"neuron_embed\" \n\
    \          )(neuron_ids) # (num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n          \n          # Expand embeddings to match batch_size\n          # (num_neurons, embedding_dim) -> (1, num_neurons, embedding_dim) -> (batch_size, num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n          neuron_embeddings_expanded = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings[jnp.newaxis, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n  \n          # 2. Prepare x for concatenation and flattening\n          # Original x: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n          # Transpose x: (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)\n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) # (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)\n          \n          # Concatenate neuron embeddings to the input features for each neuron\n          # x_transposed: (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)\n          # neuron_embeddings_expanded: (batch_size, num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n          # Result: (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon + embedding_dim)\n          x_with_embeddings = jnp.concatenate([x_transposed,\
    \ neuron_embeddings_expanded], axis=-1)\n  \n          # 3. Reshape for shared MLP processing\n          # From (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon + embedding_dim)\n          # To (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon + embedding_dim)\n          mlp_input_dim = input_horizon + self.embedding_dim\n          x_flat = jnp.reshape(x_with_embeddings, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, mlp_input_dim))\n  \n          # 4. Shared MLP layers\n          x_flat = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n          x_flat = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x_flat)\n          x_flat = nn.relu(x_flat)\n          x_flat = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x_flat)\n  \n          x_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x_flat) # Output size (32)\n  \n          # 5. Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x_output = jnp.reshape(x_flat, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x_output = jnp.transpose(x_output,\
    \ (0, 2, 1)) # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n  \n          return x_output\n  \n  \n  class NeuronEmbeddedMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n  \n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any], num_neurons: int = 71721):\n          # Pass num_neurons to the module\n          self.model = NeuronEmbeddedMLP(\n              num_neurons=num_neurons,\n              hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n\
    \          )\n          return variables\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n  \n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the NeuronEmbeddedMLP network.\"\"\"\n      # Hardcode num_neurons as it's a fixed property of ZAPBench task\n      return NeuronEmbeddedMLPWrapper(hparams, num_neurons=71721)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Experiment: Neuron Embeddings in Shared-Neuron MLP**


  Okay, so I''ve got my first experiment documented, and now I''m ready to introduce neuron embeddings into the Shared-Neuron MLP. The goal is to see if these embeddings can help the model learn neuron-specific patterns.


  Here''s the plan: I''m going to define `embedding_dim` as a new hyperparameter, and then modify the `CustomSharedNeuronMLP` (now `NeuronEmbeddedMLP` in the code) to include an `nn.Embed` layer. This will allow me to assign a unique, trainable embedding to each neuron.


  The input shape is a bit tricky, and I''ve spent some time working through the dimensions. The input `x` comes in as `(batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)`. The core idea is to transpose this to `(batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)`. I''ll generate neuron IDs, look up their embeddings, and then concatenate these embeddings to the input before flattening the data to fit into the shared MLP.


  To get the embedding working, I need to make sure I know the value of `num_neurons`. This will be used in `nn.Embed` to know how many embeddings to create. In the context of ZAPBench, I''ve hardcoded it to 71,721 as it''s a static value for this dataset.


  I''ll start by generating `neuron_ids` from 0 to `num_neurons-1`. Then, the `nn.Embed` layer will give each neuron an embedding. The shape of these embeddings is `(num_neurons, embedding_dim)`. I will expand the embeddings to have a batch dimension to get `(batch_size, num_neurons, embedding_dim)` and concatenate these to the inputs.


  I''m thinking, if the input is `(batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)`, I need to transpose it to `(batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)` first. Then I create `neuron_ids` and get their embeddings using `nn.Embed`. Next I need to expand embeddings to match the batch size. Finally, I will reshape the concatenated data for the shared MLP layer. I''ve worked out the reshape and transpose operations to make the shapes align correctly.


  I''ve also updated the `NeuronEmbeddedMLPWrapper` to pass `num_neurons` and `embedding_dim` correctly to the `NeuronEmbeddedMLP` module. I need to keep the dataclass field order in mind. I set `embedding_dim` to 16, but this is something that I can tune later. This makes the model more versatile and now includes an `nn.Embed` layer.


  The final steps are updating the `_define_hyperparameters` function to include the new `embedding_dim` hyperparameter. So I''ve got a comprehensive plan and the code is written. I''m excited to test this out!'
