parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room. I will now add a new entry to my research log (Capsule 1) detailing the results of experiment ID 357 and my revised plan for the next experiment: increasing the `hidden_size` of the core MLP.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: Global Context Dim Returns Diminish; Next: Increase MLP Capacity\"\ncontent: |\n  **Station Tick:** 171\n  **Agent Name:** Lumina I\n  \n  **1. Experiment 7: Neuron Embeddings + Learnable Per-Timestep Global Context (ID 357, Dim 16, Context 64)**\n  - **Objective:** Test if increasing `global_context_projection_dim` from 32 to 64 leads to further performance gains.\n  - **Modification:** Changed `global_context_projection_dim` to 64. `embedding_dim` and `hidden_size` remained at 16 and 128 respectively.\n  - **Results:**\n    - My Score: -0.028189291462704425\n    - Previous Best Score (ID 342, Context 32): -0.028042756175279352\n    - **Negative Result:** The score slightly worsened compared to the previous\
    \ best.\n    - **MAE Metrics Comparison (lower is better):**\n      | Metric     | Best (ID 342) | Current (ID 357) |\n      |------------|---------------|------------------|\n      | Val_MAE_1  | 0.0207        | 0.0206           | # Slight improvement\n      | Val_MAE_4  | 0.0238        | 0.0239           | # Slight worsening\n      | Val_MAE_8  | 0.0265        | 0.0268           | # Worsening\n      | Val_MAE_16 | 0.0292        | 0.0294           | # Worsening\n      | Val_MAE_32 | 0.0308        | 0.0304           | # Improvement\n    - While Val_MAE_1 and Val_MAE_32 showed some minor improvements, the overall score and other MAE metrics slightly degraded, indicating that a `global_context_projection_dim` of 32 was more optimal for this architecture.\n  \n  **2. Reflection and Next Steps: Increasing Core MLP Hidden Size**\n  - **Analysis:** Simply increasing the dimension of the global context projection did not help and even slightly hurt performance. This suggests that the current\
    \ global context dimension of 32 (from ID 342) might be adequate, or that the primary bottleneck has shifted to the capacity of the main shared MLP.\n  - The `hidden_size` of the shared MLP has remained at 128 since the first experiment (ID 282), while the input features have become significantly richer due to neuron embeddings and a learnable global context. It's plausible that the MLP now needs more capacity to process these richer inputs effectively.\n  - **Next Experiment Plan:** Increase the `hidden_size` of the core shared MLP from 128 to 256. I will revert `global_context_projection_dim` to 32 (the best-performing value from ID 342) and retain `embedding_dim` at 16.\n  - **Rationale:** A larger `hidden_size` will allow the shared MLP to learn more complex non-linear relationships from the combined temporal, embedding, and global context features, potentially unlocking further performance gains.\n  - **Hyperparameters:**\n    - `learning_rate`: 0.001\n    - `hidden_size`: 256 (Increased\
    \ from 128)\n    - `dropout_rate`: 0.1\n    - `embedding_dim`: 16\n    - `global_context_projection_dim`: 32 (Reverted to optimal from ID 342)\n  - **Hypothesis:** Providing increased capacity to the shared MLP, which now handles richer, context-aware inputs, will lead to further improvements in forecasting accuracy.\n```"
