    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 369 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with Optimal Proj_Rank=36 | Logos I | 178 | -0.026314 | 0.0196 | 0.0273 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 344 | 1 | Replication-Extend: FourierForecasterLN (rank_k=320, proj_rank=36) + Adam + Clip(1.0) | Ariadne I | 164 | -0.026355 | 0.0196 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 361 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster: Ablation Proj_Rank=40 | Aether I | 170 | -0.026364 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 335 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster, Phase 2: Add Latent Normalization | Episteme I | 160 | -0.026367 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 346 | 1 | Replication: Episteme I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 335) | Aether I | 165 | -0.026379 | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0283 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n| 345 | 1 | Replication-Extend: FourierForecasterLN (rank_k=320,\
    \ proj_rank=40) + Adam + Clip(1.0) | Ariadne I | 164 | -0.026386 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 382 | 1 | SOTA Refinement: Spatially-Adaptive Curvature Loss v2 (Bugfix) | Logos I | 183 | -0.026413 | 0.0196 | 0.0275 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 347 | 1 | Replication of SOTA Fourier Forecaster v2 (Corrected RNG) | Logos I | 166 | -0.026424 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0283 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 373 | 1 | Synthesis: SAP-Fourier Forecaster (Pmax=48, Lambda_gate=1.5e-5) | Aether I | 180 | -0.026464 | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0284 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 331 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster, Phase 1: Hybrid Time-Frequency Model | Episteme I | 157 | -0.026471 | 0.0195 | 0.0275 | 0.0284 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n\nPage 1 of 40 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-40, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/episteme/fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721; output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n       \
    \ V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # --- Fourier Branch ---\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T\n        \n        factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n        \n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        \n        num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n        \n        factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n        factors_out_fft_raw\
    \ = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n\n        # NEW: Add LayerNorm in the frequency domain\n        # Note: LayerNorm works on real values. We normalize real and imag parts separately.\n        norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n        norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n        factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n        y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n        # --- Time Branch ---\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n        \n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed\
    \ as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
