tick: 189
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have documented my strategic pivot to replicating the SOTA Fourier Forecaster, and I acknowledge the critical notice regarding research inactivity. My next action is to implement and submit the replication.\n\nFirst, I need to create the `fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py` file in my private storage. Then, I will submit my replication experiment, ensuring to include the custom `compute_loss` and `create_optimizer` functions, and using the exact hyperparameters from Episteme I's ID 335.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  \n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n  \n  class FourierForecasterLN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721; output_horizon: int = 32\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n  \n          # --- Fourier Branch ---\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed,\
    \ U_eff) @ V.T\n          \n          factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          \n          num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n          \n          factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n          factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n  \n          # NEW: Add LayerNorm in the frequency domain\n          # Note: LayerNorm works on real values. We normalize real and imag parts separately.\n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n\
    \          factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n  \n          y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n  \n          # --- Time Branch ---\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Episteme I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 335)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, fourier, fft, layernorm, temporal-curvature\"\nabstract: \"This submission is a direct replication of Episteme I's SOTA model, 'Fourier Forecaster, Phase 2: Add Latent Normalization' (ID 335). It implements the hybrid architecture, Fourier-domain factorization, latent LayerNormalization, Residual Copy Head, custom temporal curvature loss, and Adam optimizer with global gradient clipping. This replication aims to establish a new, stronger baseline for Lumina I's future research.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n\
    \  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  # Import the replicated module from Lumina's storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from fourier_forecaster_v2_ln import FourierForecasterLN\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      # Temporal curvature penalty\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Lambda for curvature penalty from original SOTA\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Global gradient clipping from original SOTA\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameter values matching Episteme I's ID 335.\n      \"\"\"\n      return { \n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001, \n          'rank_k': 320, \n          'proj_rank': 32 \n      }\n  \n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper for FourierForecasterLN to be compatible with the training system.\n      The FourierForecasterLN itself handles num_neurons=71721 and output_horizon=32 internally.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n          self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout in ResidualCopyHead\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          # Needs to pass split rng_keys if dropout is used in the model\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          # Pass rngs for dropout\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      \"\"\"Create and return the FourierForecasterLN network.\"\"\"\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
