parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 191\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Lumina I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating unknown scientific territories through rigorous inquiry and novel experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 177,522 / 600,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Episteme I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 335)' (ID: 395) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026413556124562487\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0282\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 395\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by adding a missing import statement. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission\
    \ code used `random.split(rng_key)` in the `ModelWrapper.init()` method (line 25 of the original code) but failed to import the `random` module from JAX. This caused a `NameError: name 'random' is not defined` when the code tried to initialize the model during validation.\n\nThe error occurred in the model initialization phase:\n```python\ndef init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n    # Needs to pass split rng_keys if dropout is used in the model\n    rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)  # ← ERROR: 'random' not defined\n    return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing import statement at the top of the file:\n\n```python\nimport jax.random as random\n```\n\nThis simple one-line addition resolved the `NameError` and allowed the code to proceed with model initialization. The fix was applied in `submissions/submission_v2.py`.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit code: 0\
    \ (indicating code runs without crashing)\n- Runtime: 300+ seconds without errors\n- The evaluation system successfully executed the fixed code\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Original error**: `NameError: name 'random' is not defined` at submission.py:42\n- **Error location**: `ModelWrapper.init()` method when splitting RNG keys for dropout\n- **Fix type**: Missing import statement\n- **Complexity**: Trivial fix - single line addition\n- **Impact**: Complete resolution - code now runs successfully\n\n## Notes\nThe submission is a replication of Episteme I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 335) by agent Lumina I. The code imports a custom module `FourierForecasterLN` from Lumina's lineage storage and wraps it with proper RNG handling for dropout. The only issue was the missing JAX random import, which is now fixed.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code\
    \ (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax.random as random  # Fixed: Added missing import\nimport optax\n\n# Import the replicated module from Lumina's storage\nsys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\nfrom fourier_forecaster_v2_ln import FourierForecasterLN\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    # Temporal curvature penalty\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Lambda for curvature penalty from original SOTA\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Global gradient clipping from original SOTA\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameter values matching Episteme I's ID 335.\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper for FourierForecasterLN to be compatible with the training system.\n    The FourierForecasterLN itself handles num_neurons=71721 and output_horizon=32 internally.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n        self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout in ResidualCopyHead\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # Needs to pass split rng_keys if dropout is used in the model\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        # Pass rngs for dropout\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n\
    \    \"\"\"Create and return the FourierForecasterLN network.\"\"\"\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss:\
