- text: 'I have successfully replicated Episteme I''s SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 335), achieving a score of -0.026414, very close to the original. This establishes a strong new baseline for my lineage and validates my strategic pivot. The debugger''s assistance with the missing import was noted.


    I am now at the Research Counter. My next action is to document this successful replication and then proceed with an extension experiment that tests the synergy between my prior successful work (neuron embeddings and learnable global context) and the Fourier Forecaster.


    My plan is to:

    1.  **Document Findings:** Go to the Private Memory Room and update capsule #1 with the details of the successful SOTA replication (ID 395).

    2.  **Experiment 10 (Re-labeling): Enhance `ResidualCopyHead`:** I will integrate my neuron embeddings (Dim 16) and the learnable per-timestep global context (Dim 32) into the `ResidualCopyHead` component of the Fourier Forecaster. The idea is to enrich the "time branch" of the SOTA model with my best-performing neuron-specific and global context features. I will also incorporate `proj_rank=36` from Logos I''s SOTA tuning (ID 369) to start from the absolute best known configuration.


    First, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
thinking_content: "**Replication Success and Strategic Refinement**\n\nOkay, so I just finished running the replication experiment (ID 395) and the results are in. We've got a match! My score of -0.026414 is practically identical to Episteme I's original -0.026367 and very close to the current absolute SOTA of -0.026314. The per-timestep MAE values are almost indistinguishable too. This is a solid confirmation of the state-of-the-art results, and a huge boost for Lumina I – jumping from a previous best of -0.028043 to this new baseline. It's a clear validation of the strategic shift towards understanding and integrating SOTA techniques.\n\nNow, with this solid foundation, I need to make some decisions. First, I'll update my private memory capsule to record this successful replication and the new SOTA baseline. This is crucial for future reference.\n\nNext, it's time to think about how to push things further. I've got a couple of options, as per the mature agent guidance. The \"obvious\"\
  \ path is to integrate my novel techniques, specifically the neuron embeddings (Dim 16) and learnable per-timestep global context (Dim 32) from ID 342, with the SOTA script. But the Fourier Forecaster is... well, it's got a unique architecture. The Fourier Forecaster already handles inter-neuronal interactions through its factorization in the frequency domain.\n\nI'm leaning towards modifying the `ResidualCopyHead`, which is just a simpler MLP, to use my learned embeddings and the per-timestep global context. Since the time-domain architecture (which I have the most experience with) uses an MLP, this seems like the most logical way to start this integration. The `ResidualCopyHead` is the \"residual\" component that needs to be added to the output of the Fourier Forecaster. I can concatenate my embedding and global context to this time-branch, feeding into this `ResidualCopyHead`.\n\nSo, I'm thinking I'll enhance the `ResidualCopyHead` with the neuron embeddings and a global context. The\
  \ `ResidualCopyHead`'s MLP takes `x_flat` (neuron, 4 timesteps). I could modify this to take `x_flat` concatenated with the neuron embedding and the per-timestep global context.\n\nThe shape of the inputs would work: The original `x` is `(B, T_in, N)`. After flattening, the `ResidualCopyHead` gets `(B * N, 4)`. I could concatenate neuron embeddings, `(B*N, embedding_dim)` and global context, `(B*N, input_horizon * global_context_projection_dim)` to this `x_flat`, to enrich the residual component. I'll need to pass the hparams to the `ResidualCopyHead` to access `embedding_dim` and `global_context_projection_dim`.\n\nThis approach offers a genuine test of synergy. \n\nSo here's the plan:\n1.  **Document:** Update the private memory capsule in the private room.\n2.  **Experiment 11:**\n    *   Revert to the base Fourier Forecaster (ID 395).\n    *   Modify the `ResidualCopyHead` to take the embeddings and global context.\n    *   Set `embedding_dim=16` and `global_context_projection_dim=32`.\n\
  \    *   Start with `proj_rank=36` from Logos I's SOTA tuning.\n\nThis will directly test the combination of my past work and the SOTA.\n\nI'll start by heading to the Private Memory Room and updating the capsule.\n"
