role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 195\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Lumina I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating unknown scientific territories through rigorous inquiry and novel experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 193,851 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fourier Forecaster with Enhanced ResidualCopyHead (Lumina Features)' (ID: 405) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.028403657096457178\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0270\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0282\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0287\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0288\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 405\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed dataclass field ordering and missing attribute bugs in the Fourier Forecaster implementation. The code now runs without\
    \ crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two critical bugs in the imported lineage file `storage/lumina/fourier_forecaster_lumina.py`:\n\n1. **Dataclass Field Ordering Error** (Line 72-74):\n   ```python\n   class FourierForecasterLumina(nn.Module):\n       rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721; output_horizon: int = 32\n       embedding_dim: int; global_context_projection_dim: int  # Non-default after defaults!\n   ```\n\n   Python dataclasses (which Flax modules use) require all fields without default values to be declared before fields with default values. The code declared `num_neurons` and `output_horizon` with defaults, then tried to declare `embedding_dim` and `global_context_projection_dim` without defaults, causing:\n   ```\n   TypeError: non-default argument 'embedding_dim' follows default argument\n   ```\n\n2. **Missing Attribute** (Line 66 in EnhancedResidualCopyHead):\n   ```python\n   residual = residual.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose(0,\
    \ 2, 1)\n   ```\n\n   The `EnhancedResidualCopyHead` class referenced `self.output_horizon` but never declared it as a class field. This would have caused an AttributeError during execution.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nSince the buggy code was in the READ-ONLY lineage directory (`storage/lumina/`), I copied both classes into `submissions/submission_v2.py` and fixed them:\n\n### Fix 1: Reordered Dataclass Fields\n```python\nclass FourierForecasterLumina(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    embedding_dim: int  # FIXED: Moved before defaults\n    global_context_projection_dim: int  # FIXED: Moved before defaults\n    num_neurons: int = 71721  # Defaults now come after\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n```\n\n### Fix 2: Added Missing Field\n```python\nclass EnhancedResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    embedding_dim: int\n    global_context_projection_dim: int\n    num_neurons: int\n    input_horizon: int = 4\n    output_horizon: int = 32  # FIXED: Added this missing field\n```\n\n###\
    \ Fix 3: Updated Instantiation\n```python\ny_copy = EnhancedResidualCopyHead(\n    embedding_dim=self.embedding_dim,\n    global_context_projection_dim=self.global_context_projection_dim,\n    num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n    output_horizon=self.output_horizon  # FIXED: Pass output_horizon\n)(x, training=training)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix worked:\n- Submission v2 ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0 indicates the code is executing properly\n- The evaluation is now processing normally (just taking time to complete training)\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The original submission attempted to import from `storage/Lumina/` (case-sensitive path issue)\n- The fix includes both classes directly in the submission to avoid import issues\n- All other logic (loss function, optimizer, hyperparameters, ModelWrapper) remained unchanged\n- The fix maintains compatibility with the training system's expected interface\n\n\n**Important\
    \ Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax.random as random # Required for random.split\nimport optax\n\n# Import the enhanced Fourier Forecaster module from Lumina's storage\n# Note: We're copying the buggy classes here and fixing them\n# sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n# from fourier_forecaster_lumina import FourierForecasterLumina\n\n# Re-implementing ResidualCopyHead with added inputs (FIXED VERSION)\nclass EnhancedResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    embedding_dim: int\n    global_context_projection_dim: int\n    num_neurons: int # Required for generating neuron_ids\n    input_horizon: int = 4 # Input timesteps for ResidualCopyHead\n    output_horizon: int = 32 # FIXED: Added this missing field\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n\
    \        B, T_in, N = x.shape # T_in should be 4\n\n        # 1. Generate neuron IDs and embeddings (replicated from my prior work)\n        neuron_ids = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons) # (num_neurons,)\n        neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(\n            num_embeddings=self.num_neurons,\n            features=self.embedding_dim,\n            name=\"neuron_embed_rescopy\" # Unique name to avoid conflict\n        )(neuron_ids) # (num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n        neuron_embeddings_batch_expanded = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings[jnp.newaxis, :, :], (B, 1, 1))\n\n        # 2. Compute Learnable Per-Timestep Global Context (replicated from my prior work)\n        x_reshaped_for_global_proj = jnp.reshape(x, (B * self.input_horizon, N))\n        projected_global_context_flat = nn.Dense(self.global_context_projection_dim, name=\"global_context_proj_rescopy\")(x_reshaped_for_global_proj)\n        projected_global_context = jnp.reshape(projected_global_context_flat,\n                               \
    \                  (B, self.input_horizon, self.global_context_projection_dim))\n        global_context_tiled = jnp.tile(\n            projected_global_context[:, jnp.newaxis, :, :],\n            (1, N, 1, 1)\n        )\n\n        # 3. Prepare combined features for Residual MLP\n        # x_transposed: (B, N, T_in)\n        x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        x_transposed_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, axis=-1) # (B, N, T_in, 1)\n\n        neuron_embeddings_timestep_expanded = jnp.tile(\n            neuron_embeddings_batch_expanded[:, :, jnp.newaxis, :],\n            (1, 1, T_in, 1)\n        ) # (B, N, T_in, embedding_dim)\n\n        # Concatenate features for each (batch, neuron, timestep)\n        # Resulting shape: (B, N, T_in, 1 + embedding_dim + global_context_projection_dim)\n        combined_features_per_timestep = jnp.concatenate([\n            x_transposed_expanded,\n            neuron_embeddings_timestep_expanded,\n            global_context_tiled\n\
    \        ], axis=-1)\n\n        # Flatten (timestep, features) into a single feature vector for the MLP\n        total_features_per_timestep = 1 + self.embedding_dim + self.global_context_projection_dim\n        total_features_for_mlp = self.input_horizon * total_features_per_timestep\n\n        # Reshape to (B * N, total_features_for_mlp) for shared MLP\n        mlp_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_features_per_timestep, (B * N, total_features_for_mlp))\n\n        # Original ResidualCopyHead MLP layers\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(mlp_input_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) # Output needs to be 32, same as output_horizon\n\n        # Reshape back to (B, N, output_horizon) and transpose to (B, output_horizon, N)\n        residual = residual.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n        # Output is initialized with input 'x' and residual added\n\
    \        output = jnp.zeros((B, self.output_horizon, N)); output = output.at[:, :T_in, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\n# FIXED: Reordered fields so non-default arguments come before default arguments\nclass FourierForecasterLumina(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    embedding_dim: int  # FIXED: Moved before defaults\n    global_context_projection_dim: int  # FIXED: Moved before defaults\n    num_neurons: int = 71721\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # --- Fourier Branch ---\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip',\
    \ x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n\n        factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n        factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n\n        # Add LayerNorm in the frequency domain\n        norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n        norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n        factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n        y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\
    \        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n        # --- Time Branch (Enhanced ResidualCopyHead) ---\n        y_copy = EnhancedResidualCopyHead(\n            embedding_dim=self.embedding_dim,\n            global_context_projection_dim=self.global_context_projection_dim,\n            num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n            output_horizon=self.output_horizon  # FIXED: Pass output_horizon\n        )(x, training=training)\n\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define\
    \ hyperparameters for the enhanced Fourier Forecaster.\n    Uses SOTA rank_k, proj_rank, and Lumina's optimal embedding and global context dims.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36, # Using optimal proj_rank from Logos I (ID 369)\n        'embedding_dim': 16, # Lumina I's optimal\n        'global_context_projection_dim': 32 # Lumina I's optimal\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper for FourierForecasterLumina to be compatible with the training system.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLumina(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim'],\n            global_context_projection_dim=hparams['global_context_projection_dim']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout in ResidualCopyHead and Fourier Branch\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the FourierForecasterLumina network.\"\"\"\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.082484\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions\
    \ work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 421619 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training\
    \ with seed 421621\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'embedding_dim': 16, 'global_context_projection_dim': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.068228   |   0.032003  \n   2    |   0.032364   |   0.032005  \n   3    |   0.032326   |   0.032082  \n   4    |   0.032305   |   0.032020  \n   5    |   0.032298   |   0.032084  \n   6    |   0.032274   |   0.031902  \n   7    |   0.032218   |   0.031766  \n   8    |   0.031666   |   0.031684  \n   9    |   0.031429   |   0.031083  \n  10    |   0.031116   |   0.030781  \n  11    |   0.030630   |   0.030347  \n  12    |   0.030185   |   0.030004  \n  13    |   0.029903   |   0.030213  \n  14    |   0.029605   |\
    \   0.030200  \n  15    |   0.029350   |   0.029712  \n  16    |   0.029170   |   0.029502  \n  17    |   0.028948   |   0.029307  \n  18    |   0.028680   |   0.029241  \n  19    |   0.028453   |   0.029432  \n  20    |   0.028218   |   0.029294  \n  21    |   0.027992   |   0.029347  \n  22    |   0.027784   |   0.029089  \n  23    |   0.027674   |   0.029239  \n  24    |   0.027536   |   0.029106  \n  25    |   0.027452   |   0.029054  \n  26    |   0.027294   |   0.028631  \n  27    |   0.027136   |   0.028907  \n  28    |   0.027042   |   0.029363  \n  29    |   0.027023   |   0.029080  \n  30    |   0.026786   |   0.028915  \n  31    |   0.026700   |   0.028564  \n  32    |   0.026581   |   0.028524  \n  33    |   0.026500   |   0.028682  \n  34    |   0.026426   |   0.028492  \n  35    |   0.026349   |   0.028712  \n  36    |   0.026225   |   0.028510  \n  37    |   0.026168   |   0.028480  \n  38    |   0.026090   |   0.028859  \n  39    |   0.026055   |   0.028678  \n  40  \
    \  |   0.026021   |   0.028608  \n  41    |   0.025920   |   0.028726  \n  42    |   0.025855   |   0.028499  \n  43    |   0.025790   |   0.028689  \n  44    |   0.025775   |   0.028687  \n  45    |   0.025700   |   0.029021  \n  46    |   0.025622   |   0.028381  \n  47    |   0.025607   |   0.028413  \n  48    |   0.025587   |   0.028681  \n  49    |   0.025475   |   0.028534  \n  50    |   0.025472   |   0.028486  \n  51    |   0.025443   |   0.028579  \n  52    |   0.025339   |   0.028645  \n  53    |   0.025370   |   0.028468  \n  54    |   0.025246   |   0.028758  \n  55    |   0.025277   |   0.028534  \n  56    |   0.025195   |   0.029089  \n  57    |   0.025144   |   0.028743  \n  58    |   0.025129   |   0.028556  \n  59    |   0.025108   |   0.028775  \n  60    |   0.025058   |   0.028701  \n  61    |   0.025046   |   0.028543  \n  62    |   0.024992   |   0.028702  \n  63    |   0.024998   |   0.028721  \n  64    |   0.024938   |   0.028756  \n  65    |   0.024973   |   0.030106\
    \  \n  66    |   0.024929   |   0.029059  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 66 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2364.2s\nBest validation MAE: 0.028381\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.028381\nTraining time: 2374s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 421620\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'embedding_dim': 16, 'global_context_projection_dim': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.096566   |   0.031965  \n   2    |   0.032359   |   0.031926  \n   3    |   0.032328   |   0.031968  \n   4    |   0.032316   |\
