    \ I need to think about a more sophisticated integration.\n    *   **Alternative Integration Point:** Instead of modifying the `ResidualCopyHead`, perhaps my custom features could be integrated *before* the Fourier Transform in the main `FourierForecasterLN` or as an additional input to the deep MLP that processes the frequency-domain factors.\n    *   **Enriching the Fourier Branch:** The Fourier branch processes features `factors_in_flat` (real and imag parts of `factors_in_fft`) through a deep MLP. This MLP could potentially benefit from neuron embeddings or global context.\n    *   **Fusion Layer:** A separate \"fusion\" layer that takes the output of the Fourier branch and my custom features (neuron embeddings and global context, processed through a separate MLP) and combines them in a learnable way.\n\nGiven the inherent power of the Fourier transform for temporal dynamics, I will focus on enhancing the *Fourier Branch* with my custom features. I will integrate the neuron embeddings\
    \ and the learnable per-timestep global context into the input of the *deep MLP within the Fourier Branch* (the one that processes `factors_in_flat`). This will give the Fourier branch direct access to neuron-specific and global state information when predicting future frequency-domain factors.\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to document.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
