tick: 201
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully documented the re-replication and my new plan to integrate custom features into the Fourier Branch MLP.\n\nNow, I will implement Experiment 13. This involves creating a modified `fourier_forecaster_lumina_v2.py` in my storage that includes the neuron embedding and learnable global context logic and then submitting `submission.py` that uses this new module. The key difference from my previous failed attempt (ID 405) is the *point of integration* of my custom features.\n\nFirst, I need to go to the Research Counter. Then, I will write the modified `FourierForecasterLuminaV2` module to my storage.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/fourier_forecaster_lumina_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random \n\n  # The original ResidualCopyHead remains unchanged for this experiment\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x,\
    \ training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLuminaV2(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721; output_horizon: int = 32\n      embedding_dim: int; global_context_projection_dim: int # Lumina-specific hparams\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # --- Fourier Branch ---\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1) # (B, T_freq, N) where T_freq = T_in // 2 + 1\n          x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1)) # (B, N, T_freq)\n\n          # Project input FFT factors into latent space (bip)\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T # (B, T_freq, k)\n\n          # Flatten factors for MLP input\n          factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1) # (B, T_freq, k*2)\n          \n          # --- Integrate Lumina's Custom Features here ---\n          # 1. Generate neuron IDs and embeddings (Dim 16)\n          neuron_ids = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons) # (N,)\n          neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(\n              num_embeddings=self.num_neurons,\n              features=self.embedding_dim,\n              name=\"\
    neuron_embed_fourier\" \n          )(neuron_ids) # (N, embedding_dim)\n          \n          # Expand embeddings for each batch and each frequency factor\n          # (N, embedding_dim) -> (1, N, 1, embedding_dim) -> (B, N, T_freq, embedding_dim)\n          neuron_embeddings_expanded = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings[jnp.newaxis, :, jnp.newaxis, :], \n                                                (B, 1, factors_in_flat.shape[1], 1)) # T_freq is factors_in_flat.shape[1]\n\n          # 2. Compute Learnable Per-Timestep Global Context (Dim 32)\n          # Note: global context is computed based on original time-domain input 'x' (B, T_in, N)\n          x_reshaped_for_global_proj = jnp.reshape(x, (B * T_in, N))\n          projected_global_context_flat = nn.Dense(self.global_context_projection_dim, name=\"global_context_proj_fourier\")(x_reshaped_for_global_proj)\n          projected_global_context = jnp.reshape(projected_global_context_flat,\n                                                \
    \   (B, T_in, self.global_context_projection_dim)) # (B, T_in, global_context_projection_dim)\n          \n          # This global context is in TIME domain. The Fourier MLP works in FREQUENCY domain.\n          # To integrate, we should take FFT of global context or expand it for frequency features.\n          # For a first attempt, let's simplify: take the mean of the global context across time_in\n          # as a static global context per batch. Or maybe, re-calculate per-frequency band?\n          # Let's start by calculating average global context over T_in and replicate for T_freq\n          \n          # This is tricky because factors_in_flat is (B, T_freq, k*2)\n          # We need a context per (B, T_freq) or (B)\n          \n          # Let's make a simplified *global context for the entire input sequence*, as a single vector.\n          # This is similar to ID 324, but it's specifically for the Fourier branch.\n          # Maybe the problem in 324 was the local application.\
    \ Here it is applied to global factors.\n          \n          # Option 1: Global Context for the entire sequence (B, T_in, N) -> (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n          # This needs to be tiled for factors_in_flat\n          \n          # Recalculate global context with proper reshaping for Fourier features\n          # Average global context over time-steps, for now, to get one context per batch item: (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n          mean_global_context_over_time = jnp.mean(projected_global_context, axis=1) # (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n          \n          # Tile for each frequency factor\n          # (B, global_context_projection_dim) -> (B, 1, global_context_projection_dim) -> (B, T_freq, global_context_projection_dim)\n          global_context_fft_expanded = jnp.tile(mean_global_context_over_time[:, jnp.newaxis, :], \n                                                (1, factors_in_flat.shape[1], 1))\n          \n          # The factors_in_flat has shape\
    \ (B, T_freq, k*2)\n          # The neuron_embeddings_expanded has shape (B, N, T_freq, embedding_dim)\n          # This integration point is difficult. The Fourier factors `factors_in_flat` are `(B, T_freq, k*2)`.\n          # They don't have a `num_neurons` dimension anymore. The neuron embeddings would need to be somehow integrated *before* `factors_in_fft`.\n          # `jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff)`\n          # `x_fft_transposed` is (B, N, T_freq).\n          # `U_eff` is (N, p)\n          # `V.T` is (p, k)\n          # `factors_in_fft` is (B, T_freq, k).\n\n          # Re-reading: \"project frequency-domain representations into a lower-dimensional latent space.\"\n          # This `latent space` is `factors_in_fft` (B, T_freq, k).\n\n          # Okay, the integration needs to happen differently.\n          # My original neuron embeddings and global context are per (batch, neuron, timestep).\n          # The Fourier branch processes features that are (batch,\
    \ T_freq, k) after the factorization.\n          # This factorization implicitly combines neuron information via U_eff (N, p).\n          # So, I need to integrate neuron-specific and global context *before* the factorization, or directly into the MLP that processes the factors.\n\n          # Let's reconsider. The `factors_in_flat` are the input to the deep MLP.\n          # Shape of `factors_in_flat` is `(B, T_freq * k * 2)`.\n          # This is per batch. It no longer has `N` or `T_in` dimensions.\n          # The deep MLP applies across `B` (batch dimension).\n\n          # So, I need a global representation of my Lumina features PER BATCH, not per (batch, neuron, timestep).\n          # This is actually closer to my very first *failed* global context attempt (ID 324),\n          # but here, it's combined with a different kind of feature.\n\n          # Let's take the GLOBAL context, averaged over neurons AND time,\n          # and neuron embeddings, averaged over neurons, to provide\
    \ a single, static context per batch item.\n          # This would be `(B, embedding_dim)` and `(B, global_context_projection_dim)`.\n          \n          # This is the path for integrating into the MLP that processes `factors_in_flat`.\n          # The original MLP's input `factors_in_flat` is (B, T_freq * k * 2).\n\n          # Let's prepare a combined \"Lumina Context\" per batch:\n          # 1. Neuron Embeddings: Average across neurons for a given batch.\n          #    Start with (N, embedding_dim). This is static per neuron.\n          #    We need something dynamic per batch. Perhaps a learnable aggregation across N?\n          #    Or just use a fixed set of \"global neuron embeddings\" that are averaged/pooled?\n          #    This is getting too complex.\n\n          # Reverting to simpler integration: The deep MLP on factors is (B, features) -> (B, features).\n          # I need a way to combine per-BATCH Lumina features with `factors_in_flat`.\n\n          # --- Simpler\
    \ integration for first attempt: ---\n          # 1. Compute a \"Lumina Global Features\" vector for each batch item:\n          #    - Neuron Embeddings: The neuron embeddings are fixed per neuron. It's difficult to make them \"per batch\" without aggregation.\n          #    - Global Context: From `x` (B, T_in, N), compute a *single* `global_context_vector` (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n          #      This is essentially re-using the logic from my failed ID 324, but the *application* is different.\n          #      Here it would be concatenated to `factors_in_flat`.\n\n          # Let's generate a single global context per batch from the initial time-domain `x`.\n          # This is similar to the global context from ID 324.\n\n          # Compute a *single* batch-wise global context from initial `x`\n          x_flat_for_global_context_batch = jnp.reshape(x, (B, T_in * N))\n          global_context_batch = nn.Dense(self.global_context_projection_dim, name=\"global_context_batch_fourier\"\
    )(x_flat_for_global_context_batch) # (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n\n          # Concatenate this with factors_in_flat before the deep MLP\n          # factors_in_flat: (B, T_freq * k * 2)\n          # global_context_batch: (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n          \n          # Total features for MLP: T_freq * k * 2 + global_context_projection_dim\n          combined_mlp_input = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_flat, global_context_batch], axis=-1)\n\n          # Deep MLP processes combined_mlp_input\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(combined_mlp_input); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          \n          num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n          \n          factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs,\
    \ k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n          factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n\n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n          factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n          y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n          # --- Time Branch (Original ResidualCopyHead) ---\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fourier Forecaster + Global Context in Fourier Branch MLP (Static)\"\ntags: \"sota-extension, fourier, global-context, learnable-context, fusion, neuronal-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This submission attempts to integrate a simplified global context (Dim 32) into the Fourier Forecaster's main MLP that processes frequency-domain factors. A\
    \ single global context vector is computed per batch from the entire time-domain input and then concatenated with the flattened frequency factors. This tests a more direct fusion of global information with the core Fourier prediction mechanism, using `proj_rank=36`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.random as random \n  import optax\n  \n  # Note: The FourierForecasterLuminaV2 is modified to remove the embedding for this specific experiment\n  # and only integrate the global context. The debugger will handle copying if needed.\n  \n  # The original ResidualCopyHead remains unchanged for this experiment\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n  \n  class FourierForecasterLuminaV2(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      # embedding_dim: int # Removed for this experiment\n      global_context_projection_dim: int\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n  \n          # --- Fourier Branch ---\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1) #\
    \ (B, T_freq, N)\n          x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1)) # (B, N, T_freq)\n  \n          # Project input FFT factors into latent space (bip)\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T # (B, T_freq, k)\n  \n          # Flatten factors for MLP input\n          factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1) # (B, T_freq, k*2)\n          # Reshape to (B, T_freq * k * 2)\n          factors_in_flat = jnp.reshape(factors_in_flat, (B, -1))\n          \n          # --- Integrate Lumina's Custom Global Context here ---\n          # Compute a *single* batch-wise global context from initial `x` (B, T_in, N)\n          x_flat_for_global_context_batch = jnp.reshape(x, (B, T_in * N))\n          global_context_batch = nn.Dense(self.global_context_projection_dim, name=\"global_context_batch_fourier\")(x_flat_for_global_context_batch) # (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n  \n          # Concatenate\
    \ this with factors_in_flat before the deep MLP\n          # factors_in_flat: (B, T_freq * k * 2)\n          # global_context_batch: (B, global_context_projection_dim)\n          combined_mlp_input = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_flat, global_context_batch], axis=-1)\n  \n          # Deep MLP processes combined_mlp_input\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(combined_mlp_input); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          \n          num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n          \n          factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n          factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n  \n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n       \
    \   norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n          factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n  \n          y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n  \n          # --- Time Branch (Original ResidualCopyHead) ---\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n  \n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the enhanced\
    \ Fourier Forecaster.\n      Uses SOTA rank_k, proj_rank, and Lumina's optimal global context dim.\n      \"\"\"\n      return { \n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'rank_k': 320, \n          'proj_rank': 36, # Optimal proj_rank from Aether I (ID 400)\n          'global_context_projection_dim': 32 # Lumina I's optimal\n      }\n  \n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper for FourierForecasterLuminaV2 to be compatible with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLuminaV2(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              global_context_projection_dim=hparams['global_context_projection_dim']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout in ResidualCopyHead and Fourier Branch\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params':\
    \ rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input)\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the FourierForecasterLuminaV2 network.\"\"\"\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
