    \ experiment and contains the failed logic, I need to ensure my codebase is clean. I will overwrite it with the *original* Episteme I `fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py` code, ensuring a pure SOTA replication. My previous submission (ID 413) used this clean code.\n3.  **Rethink Integration Strategy & Re-evaluate Custom Features:** My previous two attempts at integrating my features (ID 405 into `ResidualCopyHead`, ID 420 into Fourier MLP) have both failed. This raises a fundamental question: are my custom features (neuron embeddings, global context) truly complementary to the Fourier Forecaster, or are they redundant/conflicting?\n    *   The prompt `Automatic System Tips` in Message 1, tick 196, reminds me not to give up too easily. But I've now failed two attempts to integrate.\n    *   The prompt `Automatic System Tips` in Message 2, tick 172, about \"questioning and verifying other agents' claims\" might also apply to my own assumptions about the value of my \"custom features\" in this\
    \ new SOTA context.\n\n    Perhaps my neuron embeddings and global context are *not* directly compatible with the Fourier decomposition or its factorization. It might be better to:\n    *   **Simpler Fusion:** Combine the *outputs* of a vanilla Fourier Forecaster and a vanilla version of my best original model (ID 342, MLP with neuron embeddings and learnable global context) through a simple learnable linear combination, rather than trying to deeply embed features.\n    *   **Ablation of SOTA Components:** Instead of adding my features, I could try *removing* components from the SOTA model (e.g., `ResidualCopyHead`) and see if my components could replace them, or if my features make a difference in a simpler Fourier backbone without the original Time Branch. This would clarify if my features are truly synergistic or just adding noise.\n    *   **Analyze Fourier Model's Implicit Feature Learning:** The Fourier model has `U` and `V` matrices that act as learnable projections for neurons\
    \ and frequency components. These might be implicitly learning what my embeddings and global context aim to provide.\n\nFor now, the priority is to re-establish a clean SOTA baseline. I will revert `storage/Lumina/fourier_forecaster_lumina_v2.py` (which was the module used in ID 420 and before that, `fourier_forecaster_lumina.py` used in ID 405) back to the clean SOTA implementation. Then, my next experiment will be a basic replication of the current SOTA (Ariadne I's ID 411).\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to document.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
