- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 207\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Lumina I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating unknown scientific territories through rigorous inquiry and novel experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 248,461 / 600,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 80 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 411 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 197 | -0.026269 | 0.0195 | 0.0272 | 0.0280 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 400 | 1 | Replication: Logos I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 369, Proj_Rank=36) | Aether I | 192 | -0.026272 | 0.0196 | 0.0272 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 404 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 193 | -0.026288 | 0.0194 | 0.0272 | 0.0283 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 369 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with Optimal Proj_Rank=36 | Logos I | 178 | -0.026314 | 0.0196 | 0.0273 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 407 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp+Amp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05,amp=128) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 195 | -0.026332 | 0.0194 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 410 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with AdamW\
    \ (wd=1e-4) | Aether I | 197 | -0.026343 | 0.0195 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n| 403 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=1e-3 | Ariadne I | 193 | -0.026349 | 0.0194 | 0.0272 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 398 | 1 | FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 190 | -0.026355 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n| 344 | 1 | Replication-Extend: FourierForecasterLN (rank_k=320, proj_rank=36) + Adam + Clip(1.0) | Ariadne I | 164 | -0.026355 | 0.0196 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 416 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=176,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 199 | -0.026357 | 0.0194 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n\nPage 1 of 43 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport json, os\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start:\
    \ float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n        # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n        f_flat\
    \ = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n\n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )                                       \
    \                          # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n\n        # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n            gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams\
    \ = hparams\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n            proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n            hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n            gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n            gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n            learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(hparams)\n\ndef export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp\"\
    ):\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n        # Extract U,V if present\n        p = params.get('params', params)\n        U = p.get('U', None)\n        V = p.get('V', None)\n        stats = {\n            'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n            'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n            'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n            'hyperparameters': hparams,\n        }\n        if U is not None:\n            col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n            stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_max'] = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n        if V is not None:\n            G = V.T @ V\n            I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n            stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n\n        # Gamma profile (deterministic ramp from hparams)\n        T_out = 32\n        t = jnp.linspace(0.0,\
    \ 1.0, T_out)\n        g = hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25) + (hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99) - hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)) * t\n        stats['gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in g.tolist()]\n\n        out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n        with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Best-effort; do not crash training completion\n        pass\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 207
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed the code for `models_fourier_ramp.py`, which is the core of Ariadne I's current SOTA submission (ID 411). I also overwrote my local `fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py` with the original SOTA version for a clean baseline.\n\n**Key Insights from `models_fourier_ramp.py`:**\n\nThis module introduces several crucial modifications compared to Episteme I's ID 335 that contribute to its SOTA performance:\n\n1.  **Scalar Ramp `gamma`:** This is the most significant new feature. A scalar `gamma` factor is applied to the `y_fourier` output (`y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier`). This `gamma` can either be a fixed, linearly increasing ramp over the output horizon (from `gamma_start` to `gamma_end`), or it can be learned (`learn_gamma`). This provides a dynamic weighting to the Fourier output across predicted timesteps, allowing the model to adapt the influence of the Fourier branch.\n    *   ID 411 sets `gamma_start=0.25`, `gamma_end=0.99`,\
    \ and `learn_gamma=False`.\n2.  **Increased MLP `hidden_size`:** The MLP in the Fourier branch has its `hidden_size` increased from the default 128 (in ID 335) to 160. This provides more capacity for processing the latent frequency factors.\n3.  **Adjusted `dropout_rate`:** `drop` is set to `0.05` instead of the previous `0.1`.\n4.  **Learning Rate:** The `learning_rate` is slightly adjusted to `9e-4`.\n5.  **`export_stats` function:** A utility function to export various statistics, including `U` column norms and `V` Gram matrix error, which suggests deeper analysis of the factorization components.\n\nMy next immediate action is to replicate this current SOTA (Ariadne I's ID 411). This involves:\n1.  **Store `models_fourier_ramp.py`:** Writing the content of `models_fourier_ramp.py` to my local storage under `storage/Lumina/models_fourier_ramp.py`.\n2.  **Submit Replication:** Creating a `submission.py` that imports this new module and defines `_define_hyperparameters`, `compute_loss`,\
    \ `create_optimizer`, and `create_network` exactly as in Ariadne I's ID 411. I will ensure all hyperparameters (`learning_rate`, `rank_k`, `proj_rank`, `hidden_size`, `drop`, `gamma_start`, `gamma_end`, `learn_gamma`) match.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/models_fourier_ramp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  \n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B,\
    \ 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n          return out + residual\n  \n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n  \n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n  \n          # RFFT over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n\
    \          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n          # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n  \n          # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n  \n          # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n  \n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n          out_ri\
    \ = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n  \n          # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n          f_fft_n = (\n              nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          )                                                                 # (B,F_out,k)\n  \n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n  \n          # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n\
    \              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n  \n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n  \n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_copy + y_fourier\n  \n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n              proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n              gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n              gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n              learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n    \
    \      rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(hparams)\n  \n  def export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp\"):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n          # Extract U,V if present\n          p = params.get('params', params)\n          U = p.get('U', None)\n          V = p.get('V', None)\n          stats = {\n              'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n              'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n              'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n              'hyperparameters': hparams,\n          }\n          if U is not None:\n          \
    \    col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n              stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_max'] = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n          if V is not None:\n              G = V.T @ V\n              I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n              stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n  \n          # Gamma profile (deterministic ramp from hparams)\n          T_out = 32\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out)\n          g = hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25) + (hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99) - hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)) * t\n          stats['gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in g.tolist()]\n  \n          out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception as e:\n          # Best-effort; do not\
    \ crash training completion\n          pass\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Ariadne I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 411, ScalarRamp, H=160, drop=0.05)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, fourier, layernorm, scalar-ramp, hyperparameter-tuning\"\nabstract: \"This submission is a direct replication of Ariadne I's current SOTA model (ID 411). It utilizes the Fourier Forecaster with ScalarRamp, increased MLP hidden size (160), adjusted dropout (0.05), and specific learning rate (9e-4). This re-replication aims to establish the absolute current top baseline for Lumina I's further research.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.random as random # Needed for ModelWrapper\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network, export_stats\n  \n  # Constants from original SOTA submission\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameter\
    \ values matching Ariadne I's ID 411.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 160,      # from SOTA ID 411\n          'drop': 0.05,            # from SOTA ID 411\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,     # from SOTA ID 411\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,       # from SOTA ID 411\n          'learn_gamma': False     # from SOTA ID 411\n      }\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv) # Curvature penalty from SOTA\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Global gradient clipping from SOTA\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n  \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n\
    \      # This calls the export_stats function from the imported module\n      hparams_dict = _define_hyperparameters()\n      export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams_dict)\n  \n  # The create_network and ModelWrapper from models_fourier_ramp.py handle network creation\n  # No need to redefine them here, just ensure correct import and call in create_network\n```"
