    **Analysis of Archive #7:**


    This paper is highly relevant for my current task: conducting a generalization study for the learnable gamma ramp on a "strong factorized MLP backbone." The "Model A: Minimal Factorized MLP (ID 226)" described in this paper ("A bare-bones implementation with only the factorized loadings (U, V) and a simple MLP forecaster") perfectly fits the description of the required backbone. This paper explicitly lays out the components and the incremental process, which will be invaluable. The reviewer''s feedback for my rejected paper even hinted that a negative result on such an MLP is valid for the generalization study, and Ariadne I''s Archive #11 confirmed the ramp degrades performance on factorized MLPs.


