tick: 226
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed Evaluation ID 226, the \"Minimal Factorized MLP,\" which is the target backbone for my generalization study.\n\n**Analysis of ID 226 (Minimal Factorized MLP):**\n\n*   **Architecture:** It uses learnable `U` and `V` matrices for factorization, similar to the Fourier Forecaster, but operates entirely in the time domain.\n    *   `factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U) @ V.T` (Encoder)\n    *   A simple MLP (`Dense(512)->relu->Dense(32*k)`) acts as the forecaster, reshaping outputs to `(B, 32, k)`.\n    *   `y_factor = (factors_out @ V) @ U.T` (Decoder)\n*   **Simplicity:** Crucially, it explicitly states \"no dropout,\" \"no LayerNorm,\" and \"no Residual Copy Head.\" This makes it a truly bare-bones factorized MLP, ideal for isolating the effect of the gamma ramp.\n*   **Hyperparameters:** `rank_k=320`, `proj_rank=32`, `learning_rate=0.001`.\n*   **Score:** -0.029358. This is a solid baseline for a minimal\
    \ factorized MLP.\n\nMy next step is to implement this Minimal Factorized MLP, integrate my `learn_gamma=True` feature into it, and then submit it for evaluation. This will directly address the generalization study requirement for my paper.\n\nFirst, I will save the `MinimalFactorizedMLP` module into my storage. Then, I will create a new submission that uses this module, modified to include the learnable gamma ramp logic.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/minimal_factorized_mlp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random # Needed for gamma initialization\n\n  class MinimalFactorizedMLP(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      output_horizon: int = 32 # Required for gamma ramp\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25 # Required for gamma ramp (initial values)\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99   # Required for gamma ramp (initial values)\n      learn_gamma: bool = False # KEY CHANGE\
    \ for this experiment\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          \n          # No column normalization for simplicity\n          \n          # Encoder\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U) @ V.T # (B, T_in, k)\n\n          # MLP Forecaster (no dropout)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1)) # (B, T_in * k)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h) # (B, output_horizon * k)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k)) # (B, 32, k)\n\n          # No LayerNorm\n\n          # Decoder\n          y_factor = (factors_out @ V) @ U.T # (B, 32, N)\n\n          # --- Integrate\
    \ Scalar Ramp Gamma ---\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              # Initialize gamma_raw to produce an initial ramp similar to fixed gamma\n              # This ensures the learned gamma starts from a reasonable point\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, self.output_horizon, dtype=y_factor.dtype)\n              initial_g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              # Inverse sigmoid to get raw values for initialization\n              initial_gamma_raw = jnp.log(initial_g / (1.0 - initial_g))\n              \n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', lambda rng, shape: initial_gamma_raw, (self.output_horizon,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # (1, 32, 1)\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, self.output_horizon, dtype=y_factor.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None] # (1, 32, 1)\n          \n          y_factor\
    \ = gamma * y_factor # Apply gamma ramp\n          \n          # No Residual Copy Head\n          return y_factor\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Study: Minimal Factorized MLP with Learnable Gamma Ramp\"\ntags: \"generalization-study, factorized-mlp, learnable-gamma, ablation, curvature-loss-effect\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the generalization of the learnable gamma ramp (previously shown to improve Fourier Forecaster SOTA) to a 'Minimal Factorized MLP' backbone (Episteme I's ID 226). This MLP model is a bare-bones factorized architecture without residual heads, LayerNorm, or curvature loss. We apply the learnable gamma (initialized as a linear ramp) to its output. This study is crucial for a complete publication, demonstrating whether the gamma ramp is universally beneficial or architecture-specific.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.random as random\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from\
    \ minimal_factorized_mlp import MinimalFactorizedMLP # My custom module\n  \n  # Constants from original SOTA submission\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the Minimal Factorized MLP with learnable gamma.\n      Matching ID 226 for rank_k, proj_rank, learning_rate.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25, # For initialization of learnable gamma\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,   # For initialization of learnable gamma\n          'learn_gamma': True  # KEY CHANGE: Learnable gamma ramp applied\n      }\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Use default MAE loss as the Minimal Factorized MLP had no curvature loss\n      return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Use default Adam optimizer as the Minimal\
    \ Factorized MLP had no gradient clipping\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n  \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      pass # No export_stats for this minimal model\n  \n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper for MinimalFactorizedMLP to be compatible with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = MinimalFactorizedMLP(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'],\n              gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'],\n              learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False # No Dropout in MinimalFactorizedMLP\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          # MinimalFactorizedMLP has no dropout, so only params rng needed\n          # gamma_raw param is initialized within the module's __call__\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n\
    \  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the MinimalFactorizedMLP network with learnable gamma.\"\"\"\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
