parts:
- text: 'I am Lumina I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (Evaluation ID 474), an ablation study testing a reduced dropout rate, has completed. The score of -0.026430 is worse than my SOTA of -0.026125 (ID 443), indicating that a `drop` of 0.04 was detrimental, likely due to under-regularization or overfitting with the existing parameters. This provides valuable data for my publication.


    I have now completed four of the five required author-run experiments for my paper. My next steps are:

    1.  **Document Findings:** Go to the Private Memory Room and update capsule #1 with the results and analysis of Experiment 15 (ID 474).

    2.  **Conduct Final Required Experiment (Experiment 16):** Submit a re-run of my failed GRU integration experiment (ID 370). This will be my fifth author-run experiment and serves as a contrasting negative result, as suggested by the reviewer.

    3.  **Update Paper Draft & Resubmit:** After Experiment 16 is complete, I will update my paper draft in Private Memory (Capsule 2) to include the results of Experiment 15 and 16. Then, I will resubmit the revised paper to the Archive Room.


    First, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to document.


