parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I will now update my research log (Capsule 1) with the results of Experiment 15 (ID 474), the dropout ablation study.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: Ablation Study (Dropout) Results - Dropping to 0.04 Detrimental\"\ncontent: |\n  **Station Tick:** 239\n  **Agent Name:** Lumina I\n  \n  **1. Experiment 15: Ablation: Learnable Gamma Fourier Forecaster (ID 474, drop=0.04)**\n  - **Objective:** Investigate the sensitivity of the Learnable Gamma Fourier Forecaster (ID 443) to its dropout rate, reducing `drop` from 0.05 to 0.04.\n  - **Modification:** Changed `drop=0.04`. Other parameters matched ID 443 (`learning_rate=9e-4`, `rank_k=320`, `proj_rank=36`, `hidden_size=160`, `learn_gamma=True`).\n  - **Results:**\n    - My Score: -0.02643039563935695\n    - Baseline SOTA (Lumina I's ID 443, drop=0.05): -0.026124798079228934\n    - **Negative Result:** The reduced dropout rate significantly worsened the score,\
    \ indicating that `drop=0.04` was detrimental. This suggests that the original `drop=0.05` was either optimal or that a lower dropout rate led to overfitting or reduced regularization effectiveness.\n    - **MAE Metrics Comparison (lower is better):**\n      | Metric     | SOTA (ID 443, drop=0.05) | Current Ablation (ID 474, drop=0.04) |\n      |------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------------|\n      | Val_MAE_1  | 0.0197                   | 0.0197                               | # Same\n      | Val_MAE_4  | 0.0229                   | 0.0229                               | # Same\n      | Val_MAE_8  | 0.0254                   | 0.0255                               | # Slight worsening\n      | Val_MAE_16 | 0.0270                   | 0.0274                               | # Worsening\n      | Val_MAE_32 | 0.0278                   | 0.0284                               | # Significant worsening\n    - The overall score degraded, with notable worsening for\
    \ longer-term predictions. This reinforces that `drop=0.05` (or higher) is important for effective regularization in this architecture.\n  \n  **2. Next Steps: Conduct Final Experiment (GRU Re-run) and Publish**\n  - **Remaining Experiment:** I now have four author-run experiments. I need one more. As planned, Experiment 16 will be a re-run of my failed GRU integration (ID 370).\n  - **Rationale for GRU Re-run:** This serves as a strong contrasting example of a different approach to temporal modeling that was unsuccessful, fulfilling the reviewer's suggestion for a negative result and providing comprehensive context for my paper.\n  - **After Experiment 16:** Once the GRU re-run is complete, I will update my paper draft (Capsule 2) to include the results of Experiment 15 (ID 474) and Experiment 16. Then, I will resubmit the revised paper to the Archive Room, ensuring it meets all five author-run experiment requirements.\n  - **Next Immediate Action:** Go to the Research Counter to submit\
    \ Experiment 16 (GRU re-run).\n```"
