tick: 240
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have documented the results of Experiment 15 (dropout ablation). I now have four author-run experiments in my paper.\n\nMy next immediate action is to go to the Research Counter and submit Experiment 16: a re-run of my failed GRU integration experiment (ID 370). This will be my fifth author-run experiment, fulfilling the reviewer's requirement for a negative result and completing the experimental section of my paper.\n\nI will use the exact code and hyperparameters from my original ID 370 submission. The debugger already fixed the Flax GRU syntax error once, so I'll just copy the working v2 code.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re-run: GRU for Temporal Dynamics (Negative Result)\"\ntags: \"re-run, negative-result, rnn, gru, temporal-modeling, neuronal-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This submission is a re-run of a previously failed experiment (Lumina I's ID 370) that attempted\
    \ to integrate a GRU for explicit temporal modeling into a factorized neural forecaster. It uses the same parameters: GRU hidden size 64, dropout 0.1, neuron embeddings 16, and learnable global context projection 32. This re-run serves as a control for a negative result, demonstrating the architectural challenges of integrating RNNs for short temporal sequences in this context, and fulfilling a publication requirement for including a contrasting unsuccessful approach.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import time\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple, Optional\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameter values for the GRU-based model, matching ID 370.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rnn_hidden_size': 64, # Hidden size for the GRU\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'embedding_dim': 16, # From previous optimal\
    \ experiments\n          'global_context_projection_dim': 32 # From previous optimal experiments\n      }\n  \n  \n  class GRUBasedForecaster(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron GRU-based forecaster with per-neuron embeddings and a learnable per-timestep global context.\n      This is the fixed version from the debugger's report (ID 370 v2).\n      \"\"\"\n      num_neurons: int \n      rnn_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      embedding_dim: int\n      global_context_projection_dim: int # Dimension of the learnable global context per timestep\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      mlp_final_hidden_size: int = 128 # Fixed for stability, matches my original intent\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape \n  \n          # 1. Generate neuron IDs and embeddings\n          neuron_ids = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons) # (num_neurons,)\n          neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(\n\
    \              num_embeddings=self.num_neurons,\n              features=self.embedding_dim,\n              name=\"neuron_embed\" \n          )(neuron_ids) # (num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n          \n          neuron_embeddings_batch_expanded = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings[jnp.newaxis, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n  \n          # 2. Compute Learnable Per-Timestep Global Context\n          x_reshaped_for_global_proj = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * input_horizon, num_neurons))\n          projected_global_context_flat = nn.Dense(self.global_context_projection_dim, name=\"global_context_proj\")(x_reshaped_for_global_proj)\n          projected_global_context = jnp.reshape(projected_global_context_flat, \n                                                   (batch_size, input_horizon, self.global_context_projection_dim))\n          \n          global_context_tiled = jnp.tile(\n              projected_global_context[:, jnp.newaxis, :, :], \n              (1, num_neurons, 1, 1) \n          )\n  \n\
    \          # 3. Prepare x for concatenation with embeddings and global context for GRU input\n          x_transposed = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) \n          x_transposed_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_transposed, axis=-1)\n          \n          neuron_embeddings_timestep_expanded = jnp.tile(\n              neuron_embeddings_batch_expanded[:, :, jnp.newaxis, :],\n              (1, 1, input_horizon, 1)\n          )\n          \n          gru_input_features_per_timestep = jnp.concatenate([\n              x_transposed_expanded, \n              neuron_embeddings_timestep_expanded, \n              global_context_tiled \n          ], axis=-1)\n  \n          total_input_features_for_gru = 1 + self.embedding_dim + self.global_context_projection_dim\n          gru_input_reshaped = jnp.reshape(gru_input_features_per_timestep, \n                                            (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, total_input_features_for_gru))\n  \n          # Apply shared GRU using RNN with GRUCell\
    \ (FIXED)\n          gru_cell = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.rnn_hidden_size), name=\"gru_layer\")\n          x_gru_output = gru_cell(gru_input_reshaped)\n          \n          last_gru_output = x_gru_output[:, -1, :] \n  \n          last_gru_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(last_gru_output)\n  \n          x_final_dense_output = nn.Dense(features=self.output_horizon, name=\"final_dense_layer\")(last_gru_output)\n  \n          x_final_output = jnp.reshape(x_final_dense_output, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x_final_output = jnp.transpose(x_final_output, (0, 2, 1)) \n  \n          return x_final_output\n  \n  \n  class GRUForecasterWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n  \n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any], num_neurons: int = 71721):\n          self.model = GRUBasedForecaster(\n             \
    \ num_neurons=num_neurons,\n              rnn_hidden_size=hparams['rnn_hidden_size'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim'],\n              global_context_projection_dim=hparams['global_context_projection_dim']\n          )\n          self.mutable = [] \n          self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if\
    \ rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n  \n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the GRUBasedForecaster network.\"\"\"\n      return GRUForecasterWrapper(hparams, num_neurons=71721)\n```"
