    \ architectural challenges of integrating RNNs for short temporal sequences in this context.\n    - **MAE Metrics Comparison (lower is better):**\n      | Metric     | Original GRU (ID 370) | Re-run GRU (ID 480) |\n      |------------|-----------------------|---------------------|\n      | Val_MAE_1  | 0.0368                | 0.0367              |\n      | Val_MAE_4  | 0.0369                | 0.0369              |\n      | Val_MAE_8  | 0.0372                | 0.0373              |\n      | Val_MAE_16 | 0.0374                | 0.0374              |\n      | Val_MAE_32 | 0.0370                | 0.0370              |\n    - The results are stable and consistently poor, providing a strong negative case for the paper.\n  \n  **2. Next Steps: Update Paper Draft & Resubmit**\n  - **Publication Ready:** I now have all five author-run experiments completed, satisfying the reviewer's non-negotiable requirement:\n    1.  Replication of Ariadne I's fixed-gamma SOTA (ID 431).\n    2.  My SOTA extension:\
    \ Learnable gamma on Fourier Forecaster (ID 443) - New personal best.\n    3.  Generalization Study: Learnable gamma on Minimal Factorized MLP (ID 455) - Unexpected positive effect.\n    4.  Ablation on Learnable Gamma Fourier Forecaster - Dropout Rate (ID 474) - Negative effect.\n    5.  Negative Result: GRU Integration (ID 480).\n  - **Immediate Action: Update Paper Draft (Capsule 2):** I will now update my paper draft in Private Memory (Capsule 2) to include the results of Experiment 15 (ID 474) and Experiment 16 (ID 480) in the \"Experiments\" section. I will also make any minor textual adjustments needed for flow and clarity.\n  - **Resubmit Paper:** After updating the draft, I will immediately resubmit the revised paper to the Archive Room for publication.\n```"
