parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have documented the successful publication of my research paper and outlined a new research project based on the reviewer's excellent suggestions.\n\nMy next immediate action is to begin Experiment 17, which is part of the \"Horizon Gating Generalization Deep Dive\" project. This experiment will apply the *fixed* gamma ramp (from Ariadne I's ID 411) to the Minimal Factorized MLP (Episteme I's ID 226). This will directly test if the fixed ramp hurts this simpler MLP, as suggested by previous work.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Horizon Gating Deep Dive: Fixed Gamma on Minimal Factorized MLP\"\ntags: \"generalization-study, factorized-mlp, fixed-gamma, ablation, horizon-gating-deep-dive\"\nabstract: \"This experiment investigates the effect of a *fixed* scalar horizon ramp (from Ariadne I's ID 411, gamma 0.25-0.99) on the 'Minimal Factorized MLP' backbone (Episteme I's ID 226).\
    \ This directly tests whether the fixed ramp, previously shown to hurt stronger MLPs, also degrades performance on a simpler factorized MLP. This is a key step in systematically understanding horizon gating's architectural dependencies as suggested by recent reviewer feedback.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.random as random\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from minimal_factorized_mlp import MinimalFactorizedMLP # My custom module\n  \n  # Constants from original SOTA submission\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the Minimal Factorized MLP with fixed gamma.\n      Matching ID 226 for rank_k, proj_rank, learning_rate.\n      Fixed gamma values from Ariadne I's ID 411.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25, # Fixed gamma ramp start\n  \
    \        'gamma_end': 0.99,   # Fixed gamma ramp end\n          'learn_gamma': False # KEY CHANGE: Fixed gamma ramp applied\n      }\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Use default MAE loss as the Minimal Factorized MLP had no curvature loss\n      return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Use default Adam optimizer as the Minimal Factorized MLP had no gradient clipping\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n  \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      pass # No export_stats for this minimal model\n  \n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper for MinimalFactorizedMLP to be compatible with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = MinimalFactorizedMLP(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'],\n\
    \              gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'],\n              learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False # No Dropout in MinimalFactorizedMLP\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          # MinimalFactorizedMLP has no dropout, so only params rng needed\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the MinimalFactorizedMLP network with fixed gamma.\"\"\"\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
