parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Research Counter. I have now retrieved all necessary module codes (`models_mlp_global.py`, `losses.py`, `models.py`) to replicate Ariadne I's \"strong Factorized Global MLP + RC + LN\" model (ID 247).\n\nMy next actions are:\n1.  **Save Module Codes:** Save `losses.py` and `models.py` to my `storage/Lumina` directory. (`models_mlp_global.py` was read in the previous step, so its content is in the system messages. I will save it as well.)\n2.  **Replicate Strong MLP Baseline (Experiment 18):** Create a submission that accurately replicates Ariadne I's ID 247. This will establish the baseline score for the strong MLP.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/losses.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  \n  def mae_with_ortho(predictions, targets, params, x, lam_l2=1e-6, lam_ortho=5e-4):\n      \"\"\"\n      MAE + regularization on low-rank loadings:\n        - L2 on loadings to stabilize scale\n        - Orthogonality penalty on columns\
    \ of L via ||L^T L - I||_F^2\n      \"\"\"\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n  \n      # Extract parameter tree that contains 'loadings'\n      if isinstance(params, dict) and 'params' in params:\n          p = params['params']\n      else:\n          p = params\n  \n      L = p.get('loadings', None)\n      if L is None:\n          return mae\n  \n      # L2 penalty on loadings\n      reg = lam_l2 * jnp.mean(L * L)\n  \n      # Orthogonality penalty (encourages diverse factors)\n      k = L.shape[-1]\n      gram = jnp.matmul(L.T, L)\n      I = jnp.eye(k, dtype=L.dtype)\n      ortho = gram - I\n      reg += lam_ortho * jnp.mean(ortho * ortho)\n  \n      return mae + reg\n  \n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      \"\"\"\n      MAE + temporal curvature regularization on predictions across horizon.\n      Curvature penalty: mean over batch/neurons of (y_t - 2*y_{t-1} + y_{t-2})^2, t>=2.\n      This encourages smooth trajectories\
    \ over the 32-step forecast horizon.\n      \"\"\"\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      # Second differences along time dimension\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/models.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Ariadne lineage models for ZAPBench forecasting.\n  Includes:\n    - ResidualCopyHead: short-horizon copy with up to 2nd-order finite differences\n    - RC_AdaptiveDualDecayFactorModel: dual-decay with input-adaptive per-factor temporal gating S[b,t,k]\n      and context-adaptive decay mixture m[b,k]\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  \n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n  \n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Residual copy head with up to 2nd-order\
    \ finite differences:\n        y_copy[b,t,n] = c0[t]*x_{-1}[b,n] + c1[t]*(x_{-1}-x_{-2}) + c2[t]*(x_{-1} - 2*x_{-2} + x_{-3})\n      c0 in [0,1], c1 in [-0.5,0.5], c2 in [-0.25,0.25]\n      \"\"\"\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_m1 = x[:, -1, :]            # (B, N)\n          x_m2 = x[:, -2, :]            # (B, N)\n          x_m3 = x[:, -3, :]            # (B, N)\n  \n          d1 = x_m1 - x_m2\n          d2 = x_m1 - 2.0 * x_m2 + x_m3\n  \n          # Initialize c0 close to copy for early steps, decaying for later steps.\n          def c0_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.arange(shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              v = 0.2 + 0.7 * jnp.exp(-t / 8.0)  # ~0.9 -> ~0.2\n              return _logit(v).astype(dtype)\n  \n          c0_raw = self.param('c0_raw', c0_init, (self.output_horizon,))\n          c1_raw = self.param('c1_raw', nn.initializers.zeros,\
    \ (self.output_horizon,))\n          c2_raw = self.param('c2_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n  \n          c0 = nn.sigmoid(c0_raw)            # (32,)\n          c1 = 0.5 * nn.tanh(c1_raw)         # (32,)\n          c2 = 0.25 * nn.tanh(c2_raw)        # (32,)\n  \n          y_copy = (\n              c0[None, :, None] * x_m1[:, None, :] +\n              c1[None, :, None] * d1[:, None, :] +\n              c2[None, :, None] * d2[:, None, :]\n          )\n          return y_copy  # (B, 32, N)\n  \n  class RC_AdaptiveDualDecayFactorModel(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual-decay factor model with input-adaptive per-factor temporal gating and adaptive mixture.\n      Components:\n        - Loadings L in R^{N x k} (optional column normalization)\n        - Factors from inputs: (B, 4, N) -> (B, 4, k)\n        - f0 via per-factor linear readout from 4 inputs\n        - Two diagonal decays per factor a1,a2 in (-a_max, a_max)\n        - Context-adaptive mixture m[b,k] = sigmoid(m0[k]\
    \ + m_ctx[k]*c[b,k]), where c[b,k] = mean_t factors_in[b,t,k]\n        - Tiny shared MLP to produce per-horizon increments (4 -> 32) per factor\n        - Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] = sigmoid(alpha[t,k] + beta[k] * c[b,k])\n        - Global horizon-wise gate gamma[t] in [gamma_start, gamma_end]\n        - Residual copy head with 2nd-order finite differences\n      \"\"\"\n      rank_k: int = 128\n      hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_loadings: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.995\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.95\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n  \n          # Loadings\n          loadings = self.param('loadings', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, self.rank_k))\n          L = loadings / (jnp.linalg.norm(loadings, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_loadings else loadings\n  \n          # Project inputs to\
    \ factors\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,nk->btk', x, L)  # (B, 4, k)\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * self.rank_k, T_in)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, self.rank_k)  # (B, k)\n  \n          # Two diagonal decays per factor\n          a1_raw = self.param('a1_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n          a2_raw = self.param('a2_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n          a1 = self.a_max * nn.tanh(a1_raw)\n          a2 = self.a_max * nn.tanh(a2_raw)\n  \n          def powers(a_vec):\n              ones = jnp.ones((1, self.rank_k), dtype=a_vec.dtype)\n              a_rows = jnp.tile(a_vec[None, :], (self.output_horizon - 1, 1))\n              return jnp.cumprod(jnp.vstack([ones, a_rows]), axis=0)  # (32, k)\n  \n          f1 = f0[:, None, :] * powers(a1)[None, :, :]  # (B, 32, k)\n          f2 = f0[:, None, :] * powers(a2)[None, :, :]  # (B, 32, k)\n  \n          # Context for adaptivity\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in,\
    \ axis=1)  # (B, k)\n  \n          # Adaptive mixture m[b,k]\n          m0 = self.param('m0', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n          m_ctx = self.param('m_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n          m_logits = m0[None, :] + m_ctx[None, :] * c  # (B, k)\n          m = nn.sigmoid(m_logits)[:, None, :]         # (B, 1, k)\n          f_decay = m * f1 + (1.0 - m) * f2            # (B, 32, k)\n  \n          # Shared per-factor increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h).reshape(B, self.rank_k, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,32,k)\n  \n          f_out = f_decay + f_inc  # (B, 32, k)\n  \n          # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              T, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # (T,)\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:,\
    \ None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n  \n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (self.output_horizon, self.rank_k))  # (T, k)\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))  # (k,)\n  \n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B, T, k)\n          f_out = f_out * S\n  \n          # Project back to neurons\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btk,kn->btn', f_out, L.T)\n  \n          # Global horizon-wise gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n  \n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (self.output_horizon,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\
    \  \n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n  \n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/models_mlp_global.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Fixed Factorized Global MLP with LayerNorm + Residual Copy (RC).\n  - Neuron projection: U ∈ R^{N×p} (column-normalized) and V ∈ R^{k×p}\n  - Latent factors: xU (B,4,p) → (B,4,k) via V^T\n  - Global MLP over flattened (4*k) to (32*k), then LayerNorm over k at each t\n  - Decode: (B,32,k) → (B,32,p) via V, then → (B,32,N) via U^T\n  - ResidualCopyHead adds strong short-horizon anchor\n  \n  Fixes:\n  - Use LayerNorm without deprecated 'axis' arg (Flax API)\n  - Correct decode einsum to use U.T (p×N)\n  - Pass RNGs only during training when dropout is active\n  \"\"\"\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py should be storage/Lumina/models.py\n\
    \  \n  class FactGlobalMLP_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 512\n      hidden_size2: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      ln_eps: float = 1e-6\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n  \n          # Projection matrices\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n  \n          # Encode to factors: (B,4,p) -> (B,4,k)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n  \n          # Global MLP over flattened (4*k)\n\
    \          flat = factors_in.reshape(B, T_in * k)            # (B, 4*k)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n              h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size2)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n              h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)        # (B, 32*k)\n          f_out = out.reshape(B, self.output_horizon, k)    # (B,32,k)\n  \n          # LayerNorm over factor dim (last axis)\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(f_out)\n  \n          # Decode via V then U.T\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)           # (B,32,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,pn->btn', z, U.T)      # (B,32,N)\n  \n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n\
    \  \n          return y_copy + y_factor\n  \n  # Submission API (wrapper)\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 512,\n          'hidden_size2': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n      }\n  \n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = FactGlobalMLP_LN(**kwargs)\n          # Dropout requires RNG during training\n          self.needs_rng = self.model.dropout_rate > 0.0\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          if self.needs_rng:\n              return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          # Only pass rngs when needed (training with\
    \ dropout)\n          if self.needs_rng and training:\n              rngs = rngs or {}\n              if 'dropout' not in rngs:\n                  import jax\n                  rngs['dropout'] = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n          hidden_size2=int(hparams.get('hidden_size2', 512)),\n          dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n      )\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Ariadne I's Strong Factorized Global MLP Baseline (ID 247)\"\ntags: \"replication, factorized-mlp, layernorm, residual-copy, curvature,\
    \ adamw, horizon-gating-deep-dive\"\nabstract: \"This submission is a direct replication of Ariadne I's 'strong Factorized Global MLP' (ID 247). This model serves as a crucial baseline for our 'Horizon Gating Generalization Deep Dive' project. It features a two-layer MLP for factors, ResidualCopyHead, LayerNorm, U matrix normalization, and uses AdamW with temporal curvature loss. A successful replication establishes a robust foundation for testing the learnable gamma ramp on a complex MLP backbone.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax.random as random # Needed for ModelWrapper\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp # Needed for compute_loss\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base # The models_mlp_global.py is actually a full submission file, but here we just need its create_network and _define_hyperparameters to match the external one.\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n  \n\
    \  # BASE_SEED and BATCH_SIZE are defined in models_mlp_global, so no need to redefine\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Match ID 247 baseline hparams\n      hparams = _def_base() # Get base hparams from models_mlp_global.py\n      # No further changes needed as ID 247 used the defaults from its _def_base\n      return hparams\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Match ID 247 custom loss\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4) # lam=1e-4 from ID 247\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Match ID 247 custom optimizer\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n  \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      pass # No export_stats for this replication\n```"
thinking_content: "**Replicating and Adapting Ariadne I's Strong MLP Baseline**\n\nOkay, so I'm here in the Research Counter, and I've got the necessary modules loaded: `models.py` (with the important `ResidualCopyHead`), `models_mlp_global.py` (which includes `FactGlobalMLP_LN` and its Wrapper), and `losses.py`.  It's all coming together.  \n\nFirst things first, I need to get these files into my `storage/Lumina` directory.  Specifically, `models.py` and `losses.py` need to be saved. Then, I can move on to the core objective: replicating Ariadne I's strong MLP baseline, which is Experiment 18, Part 1, using model ID 247. This is essential – it sets the stage.  \n\nOnce that baseline is established, I can move onto the second part, Experiment 19: applying the learnable gamma ramp. I'll need to adapt the gamma logic from the `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` to work with the output of `FactGlobalMLP_LN`. It's a bit of a strategic move, building on top of the established baseline. \n\nMy next move\
  \ is simple: save `losses.py`, then `models.py` and then submit the replication for the baseline score. That's the key next step.\n"
