tick: 263
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have documented the successful replication of the strong Factorized Global MLP baseline.\n\nMy next immediate action is to go to the Research Counter to modify my local `models_mlp_global.py` to integrate the learnable gamma ramp logic. Then I will submit Experiment 19, which applies the learnable gamma to this strong MLP backbone.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/models_mlp_global.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Fixed Factorized Global MLP with LayerNorm + Residual Copy (RC).\n  - Neuron projection: U ∈ R^{N×p} (column-normalized) and V ∈ R^{k×p}\n  - Latent factors: xU (B,4,p) → (B,4,k) via V^T\n  - Global MLP over flattened (4*k) to (32*k), then LayerNorm over k at each t\n  - Decode: (B,32,k) → (B,32,p) via V, then → (B,32,N) via U^T\n  - ResidualCopyHead adds strong short-horizon anchor\n\n  Fixes:\n  - Use LayerNorm without deprecated 'axis' arg (Flax API)\n  - Correct decode\
    \ einsum to use U.T (p×N)\n  - Pass RNGs only during training when dropout is active\n  \"\"\"\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.random as random # Needed for gamma initialization\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional # Added Optional for gamma parameters\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/Lumina/models.py\n  \n  def _logit(p): # Copied from models.py for internal use, if needed for initialization\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class FactGlobalMLP_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 512\n      hidden_size2: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      ln_eps: float = 1e-6\n      # New parameters for learnable gamma\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n\n          # Projection matrices\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # Encode to factors: (B,4,p) -> (B,4,k)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Global MLP over flattened (4*k)\n          flat = factors_in.reshape(B, T_in * k)            # (B, 4*k)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n              h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size2)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n\
    \          if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n              h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)        # (B, 32*k)\n          f_out = out.reshape(B, self.output_horizon, k)    # (B,32,k)\n\n          # LayerNorm over factor dim (last axis)\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(f_out)\n\n          # Decode via V then U.T\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)           # (B,32,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,pn->btn', z, U.T)      # (B,32,N)\n\n          # --- Integrate Scalar Ramp Gamma ---\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              # Initialize gamma_raw to produce an initial ramp similar to fixed gamma\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, self.output_horizon, dtype=y_factor.dtype)\n              initial_g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              # Inverse sigmoid to get raw values for initialization\n              initial_gamma_raw\
    \ = _logit(initial_g) # Use _logit copied above\n              \n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', lambda rng, shape: initial_gamma_raw, (self.output_horizon,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # (1, 32, 1)\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, self.output_horizon, dtype=y_factor.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None] # (1, 32, 1)\n          \n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor # Apply gamma ramp\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n\n  # Submission API (wrapper)\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters(\n      learning_rate: float = 0.001,\n      rank_k: int = 320,\n      proj_rank: int = 32,\n      hidden_size: int = 512,\n      hidden_size2: int = 512,\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1,\n     \
    \ normalize_u: bool = True,\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25, # New parameter\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99,   # New parameter\n      learn_gamma: bool = False  # New parameter\n  ):\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': learning_rate,\n          'rank_k': rank_k,\n          'proj_rank': proj_rank,\n          'hidden_size': hidden_size,\n          'hidden_size2': hidden_size2,\n          'dropout_rate': dropout_rate,\n          'normalize_u': normalize_u,\n          'gamma_start': gamma_start,\n          'gamma_end': gamma_end,\n          'learn_gamma': learn_gamma\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          # Extract gamma parameters if present in kwargs\n          gamma_start = kwargs.pop('gamma_start', 0.25)\n          gamma_end = kwargs.pop('gamma_end', 0.99)\n          learn_gamma = kwargs.pop('learn_gamma', False)\n\n          self.model = FactGlobalMLP_LN(\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end,\n    \
    \          learn_gamma=learn_gamma,\n              **kwargs\n          )\n          # Dropout requires RNG during training\n          self.needs_rng = self.model.dropout_rate > 0.0\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          if self.needs_rng:\n              return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          # Only pass rngs when needed (training with dropout)\n          if self.needs_rng and training:\n              rngs = rngs or {}\n              if 'dropout' not in rngs:\n                  import jax\n                  rngs['dropout'] = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return Wrapper(\n\
    \          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n          hidden_size2=int(hparams.get('hidden_size2', 512)),\n          dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)), # Passed to Wrapper constructor\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),     # Passed to Wrapper constructor\n          learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False)) # Passed to Wrapper constructor\n      )\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Horizon Gating Deep Dive: Learnable Gamma on Strong Factorized MLP\"\ntags: \"generalization-study, factorized-mlp, learnable-gamma, ablation, horizon-gating-deep-dive\"\nabstract: \"This experiment applies a *learnable* scalar horizon ramp (from Lumina I's SOTA, ID 443) to Ariadne I's 'strong\
    \ Factorized Global MLP' backbone (replicated ID 500). This directly tests whether the learnable ramp can improve performance on a more complex, already optimized MLP, as suggested by recent reviewer feedback. This is a crucial step in understanding the architectural dependencies of horizon gating, contrasting with the Fourier Forecaster and Minimal MLP results.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax.random as random\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base, BASE_SEED, BATCH_SIZE\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Get base hparams for ID 247 from models_mlp_global.py's _def_base\n      hparams = _def_base() \n      # Override gamma parameters for this experiment\n      hparams['gamma_start'] = 0.25 # For initialization of learnable gamma\n      hparams['gamma_end'] = 0.99   # For initialization\
    \ of learnable gamma\n      hparams['learn_gamma'] = True # KEY CHANGE: Enable learnable gamma\n      return hparams\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n  \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      pass # No export_stats for this experiment\n```"
