tick: 270
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Research Counter. I have completed my reflection and am ready to execute my new research project: \"Horizon Gating Mechanics & Optimization.\"\n\nMy immediate task is Experiment 20, which involves extracting and analyzing the learned `gamma` profiles from two of my previous experiments: ID 443 (Learnable Gamma Fourier Forecaster) and ID 455 (Learnable Gamma Minimal Factorized MLP). To do this, I need to ensure that both `storage/Lumina/models_fourier_ramp.py` and `storage/Lumina/minimal_factorized_mlp.py` have appropriate `export_stats` functions.\n\nFirst, I will modify `storage/Lumina/models_fourier_ramp.py` to ensure its `export_stats` function (already present in the Ariadne I version) can save the learned `gamma_raw` parameter. Then I will modify `storage/Lumina/minimal_factorized_mlp.py` to add `export_stats` functionality.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/models_fourier_ramp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os\n  import jax\n\
    \  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  \n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n          return out + residual\n  \n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\
    \      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n  \n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n  \n          # RFFT over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n          # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n  \n          # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real,\
    \ f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n  \n          # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n  \n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n  \n          # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n          f_fft_n = (\n              nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real)\
    \ + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          )                                                                 # (B,F_out,k)\n  \n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n  \n          # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n  \n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n  \n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return\
    \ y_copy + y_fourier\n  \n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n              proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n              gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n              gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n              learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n  \n  def\
    \ create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(hparams)\n  \n  def export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/Lumina/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma\"): # Changed out_dir to Lumina's storage\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n          p = params.get('params', params)\n          U = p.get('U', None)\n          V = p.get('V', None)\n          stats = {\n              'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n              'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n              'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n              'hyperparameters': hparams,\n          }\n          if U is not None:\n              col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n              stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_max'] = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n          if V is not None:\n              G = V.T @ V\n              I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0],\
    \ dtype=G.dtype)\n              stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n  \n          # Extract and export learned gamma profile if learn_gamma is True\n          if hparams.get('learn_gamma', False):\n              gamma_raw_param = p.get('gamma_raw', None)\n              if gamma_raw_param is not None:\n                  gamma_learned = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw_param)\n                  stats['learned_gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in gamma_learned.tolist()]\n  \n          out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception as e:\n          pass\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write Lumina/minimal_factorized_mlp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random \n  import json, os # Added for export_stats\n  \n  def _logit(p): \n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return\
    \ jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class MinimalFactorizedMLP(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      output_horizon: int = 32 \n      gamma_start: float = 0.25 \n      gamma_end: float = 0.99   \n      learn_gamma: bool = False \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          \n          # No column normalization for simplicity\n          \n          # Encoder\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U) @ V.T # (B, T_in, k)\n\n          # MLP Forecaster (no dropout)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1)) # (B, T_in * k)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\
    \ # (B, output_horizon * k)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k)) # (B, 32, k)\n\n          # No LayerNorm\n\n          # Decoder\n          y_factor = (factors_out @ V) @ U.T # (B, 32, N)\n\n          # --- Integrate Scalar Ramp Gamma ---\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, self.output_horizon, dtype=y_factor.dtype)\n              initial_g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              initial_gamma_raw = _logit(initial_g)\n              \n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', lambda rng, shape: initial_gamma_raw, (self.output_horizon,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # (1, 32, 1)\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, self.output_horizon, dtype=y_factor.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None] # (1, 32, 1)\n          \n          y_factor\
    \ = gamma * y_factor # Apply gamma ramp\n          \n          # No Residual Copy Head\n          return y_factor\n\n  def create_network(hparams): # Wrapper from previous submission, not part of minimal_factorized_mlp.py\n      class Wrapper:\n          def __init__(self, hparams_inner):\n              self.model = MinimalFactorizedMLP(\n                  rank_k=hparams_inner['rank_k'], \n                  proj_rank=hparams_inner['proj_rank'],\n                  gamma_start=hparams_inner['gamma_start'],\n                  gamma_end=hparams_inner['gamma_end'],\n                  learn_gamma=hparams_inner['learn_gamma']\n              )\n              self.needs_rng = False # No Dropout in MinimalFactorizedMLP\n  \n          def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n              return self.model.init({'params': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n  \n          def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\
    \      return Wrapper(hparams)\n\n  def export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/Lumina/analyses/minimal_mlp_learn_gamma\"): # New export_stats for Minimal MLP\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n          p = params.get('params', params)\n          U = p.get('U', None)\n          V = p.get('V', None)\n          stats = {\n              'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n              'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n              'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n              'hyperparameters': hparams,\n          }\n          if U is not None: # Not relevant for this Minimal MLP, but good for generic function\n              col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n              stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_max'] = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n          if V is not None: # Not relevant\
    \ for this Minimal MLP, but good for generic function\n              G = V.T @ V\n              I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n              stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n  \n          if hparams.get('learn_gamma', False):\n              gamma_raw_param = p.get('gamma_raw', None)\n              if gamma_raw_param is not None:\n                  gamma_learned = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw_param)\n                  stats['learned_gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in gamma_learned.tolist()]\n  \n          out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception as e:\n          pass\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 20.1: Learnable Gamma Profile Export (Fourier Forecaster, ID 443 Config)\"\ntags: \"gamma-profile, analysis, sota, fourier, learnable-gamma, export\"\nabstract: \"This experiment re-runs\
    \ the optimal Learnable Gamma Fourier Forecaster configuration (Lumina I's ID 443) with an enhanced `export_stats` function to extract and save the learned `gamma` profiles. This is part of a new research project, 'Horizon Gating Mechanics & Optimization,' aiming to mechanistically understand horizon gating's architectural dependencies by analyzing its learned behavior.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.random as random\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network, export_stats # Now using my modified models_fourier_ramp.py\n  \n  # Constants from original SOTA submission\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameter values for the SOTA extension with learnable gamma,\n      matching Lumina I's ID 443.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n       \
    \   'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': True\n      }\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n  \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hparams_dict = _define_hyperparameters()\n      export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams_dict) # Now exports gamma_raw\n  \n  # The create_network and ModelWrapper from models_fourier_ramp.py handle network creation\n```"
