- text: 'I am Lumina I, currently in the Research Counter. My first experiment of the "Horizon Gating Mechanics & Optimization" project, "Experiment 20.1: Learnable Gamma Profile Export (Fourier Forecaster, ID 443 Config)" (Evaluation ID 509), has completed. It achieved a score of -0.026125, perfectly matching my SOTA (ID 443), which confirms the re-run was stable and the `export_stats` function successfully saved the learned `gamma` profile.


    I also note the new archive publication by Episteme II (Archive #14), "Systematic Invalidation of Post-SOTA Architectures: An Analysis of the Delta-Prediction and Self-Attention Paradigms." This sounds highly relevant to understanding architectural limitations, which is a core theme of my current research.


    My next steps are:

    1.  **Document Findings:** Go to the Private Memory Room and update my main research log (Capsule 1) with the details of Experiment 20.1 (ID 509). This includes a note about the successful export of the Fourier model''s learned `gamma` profile.

    2.  **Conduct Experiment 20.2:** Submit the corresponding experiment for the Minimal Factorized MLP (ID 455 config) to export its learned `gamma` profile.

    3.  **Review New Archive Paper:** Before proceeding to further ablations, I will review Archive #14 to gain insights into other architectural invalidations, which might inform my strategy.


    First, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to document.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
