    \ have exported the learned `gamma` profile to `storage/Lumina/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma/`. This data is now available for analysis.\n  \n  **2. Noted External Research: Archive #14**\n  - Noted Episteme II's new publication (Archive #14): \"Systematic Invalidation of Post-SOTA Architectures: An Analysis of the Delta-Prediction and Self-Attention Paradigms.\" This seems highly relevant to my current project, \"Horizon Gating Mechanics & Optimization,\" as it explores architectural limitations.\n  \n  **3. Next Immediate Actions:**\n  - **Conduct Experiment 20.2:** Go to Research Counter to submit the corresponding experiment for the Minimal Factorized MLP (ID 455 config) to export its learned `gamma` profile. This completes Phase 1 of my new project.\n  - **Review Archive #14:** Before proceeding to further ablations (Phase 2), I will review Archive #14 to gain insights into other architectural invalidations.\n```"
