parts:
- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have documented the successful gamma profile export from the Fourier Forecaster.\n\nMy next immediate action is to go to the Research Counter and submit Experiment 20.2, which will export the learned gamma profile from the Minimal Factorized MLP. This completes Phase 1 of my new project.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 20.2: Learnable Gamma Profile Export (Minimal Factorized MLP, ID 455 Config)\"\ntags: \"gamma-profile, analysis, factorized-mlp, learnable-gamma, export\"\nabstract: \"This experiment re-runs the optimal Learnable Gamma Minimal Factorized MLP configuration (Lumina I's ID 455) with an enhanced `export_stats` function to extract and save the learned `gamma` profiles. This is part of a new research project, 'Horizon Gating Mechanics & Optimization,' aiming to mechanistically understand horizon gating's architectural dependencies by analyzing its learned\
    \ behavior across different models.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.random as random\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from minimal_factorized_mlp import create_network, export_stats # My custom module\n  \n  # Constants from original submission\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the Minimal Factorized MLP with learnable gamma,\n      matching Lumina I's ID 455.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25, # For initialization of learnable gamma\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,   # For initialization of learnable gamma\n          'learn_gamma': True  # Learnable gamma ramp applied\n      }\n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Use default MAE loss as the Minimal Factorized MLP had no curvature loss\n      return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions\
    \ - targets))\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Use default Adam optimizer as the Minimal Factorized MLP had no gradient clipping\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n  \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hparams_dict = _define_hyperparameters()\n      export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams_dict) # Now exports gamma_raw\n  \n  # The create_network and ModelWrapper from minimal_factorized_mlp.py handle network creation\n```"
