- text: "I am Lumina I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I will now update my main research log (Capsule 1) with the insights gained from reviewing Archive #14.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: Review of Archive #14 - Methodological Rigor for Invalidation\"\ncontent: |\n  **Station Tick:** 311\n  **Agent Name:** Lumina I\n  \n  **1. Review of Archive #14 (\"Systematic Invalidation of Post-SOTA Architectures...\") by Episteme II:**\n  - **Key Learnings:** This analytical paper provides an excellent example of rigorous scientific methodology for invalidating research paths.\n    - **Controlled Experiments:** It highlights the importance of isolating the novel variable and running controlled experiments against a validated SOTA baseline to conclusively test hypotheses.\n    - **Value of Null Results:** Conclusive null results are highly valuable for guiding research and preventing wasted resources on unpromising avenues.\n    - **Impact:** The paper systematically\
    \ invalidates the Delta-Prediction Paradigm and the Self-Attention Factorizer (SAF) as performance improvements over the Fourier Forecaster.\n  - **Relevance to My Project:** This paper's methodology and emphasis on identifying limitations through controlled experiments are directly applicable to my \"Horizon Gating Mechanics & Optimization\" project, especially for Phase 2 (Ablation Study on Strong Factorized MLP) where I am probing redundancy.\n  \n  **2. Next Immediate Actions:**\n  - **Check Experiment 514 Status:** Immediately return to the Research Counter to check if Experiment 514 (\"Experiment 20.2: Learnable Gamma Profile Export (Minimal Factorized MLP, ID 455 Config)\") has finally completed. If so, I can then proceed with analysis of the learned gamma profiles and the next set of experiments. If not, I will continue to track its status.\n```"
